Package: wifi-cli
Version: 0.1.0
Section: net
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: bash (>= 4.3), iw, wpasupplicant, systemd, iproute2
Recommends: wireless-regdb
Maintainer: Elliott <elliott@hstg.io>
Homepage: https://github.com/HSTG-IO/wifi-cli
Description: scan, pick and connect to Wi-Fi from a headless shell
 Provides a single `wifi` command: run it, it scans for networks, shows a
 numbered list, asks for a password and connects. Persists across reboots via
 wpa_supplicant@<iface> and systemd-networkd. Falls back to nmcli when
 NetworkManager owns the interface. Plain bash; no daemon.
